              },
              "replacement": "  // arguments, replacing UnscaledMaximum(num_arguments). AccurateRNorm needs a\n  // tighter upper bound than AccurateNorm because if the inputs are too large,\n  // the reciprocal norm rho \u003d 1 / norm falls below Tiny(), causing\n  // fma(-rho, rho, r) to underflow even when sum_of_squares itself does not\n  // overflow. The reciprocal norm then is at least Tiny() which keeps the\n  // rounding error of its square exact.\n"
